{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"veryblue-pygmyish-swordfish","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Discovered while fixing bug c49a-225d-2bc0-4478 (perplexed-jeanlike-kakarikis).\n\nThe check_wall_clock_asserts gate did not flag test_narrow_operation_persists_the_same_bytes_as_the_legacy_sequence, which flaked on a wall-clock boundary. The flake mechanism is INDIRECT: the test never asserts on a timestamp directly. Instead it asserts byte-equality between two files independently produced by BindingStore.save(), and each save stamps created_at/updated_at from the wall clock in product code (BindingLifecycle.bind_confirm -> _now_iso). When the two builds straddle a 1-second boundary the serialized bytes differ.\n\nThis is a gate blind spot: a byte/text-equality assertion between two artifacts that each embed wall-clock state (across separate builds, without a frozen clock) is a latent flake the current heuristic misses.\n\nPossible directions (design decision, not yet scoped):\n- Extend check_wall_clock_asserts to flag read_bytes()/read_text() equality assertions between two separately-produced artifacts in a test that does not freeze the clock (monkeypatch _now_iso / utc_now_iso), or\n- Audit the other cross-artifact byte-equality tests in tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/ (test_binding_lifecycle, test_get_rotation_*, test_binding_recovery, test_alert_store_atomic_write) for the same latent pattern.\n\nAcceptance criteria to be refined during planning; filing now as discovered follow-up so the gate gap is tracked rather than lost.","id":"f8c6-6ab3-ca81-4d30","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"check_wall_clock_asserts misses transitive timestamp flakes (byte-equality of independently-timestamped saves)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787941522681366001,"uuid":"8e72c546-4dfa-4f52-b2c2-5071655ff1d1"}